  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA n2000 (config_001) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while image-only with ResNet50 (config_010) is weak at 20.8%, confirming RNA is the dominant signal. The only RNA encoder tested so far is a linear method (PCA). Question: Does a learned nonlinear RNA representation (scvi_n200) improve over PCA n2000? This experiment (config_004) is a single-variable change from config_001—only the RNA encoder changes—so any accuracy shift can be cleanly attributed to the encoder. Rationale: With 7 experiments remaining, establishing whether a better RNA representation can push accuracy above ~48% is the highest-leverage question before investing in multiprofile, image, or fusion experiments. If scvi_n200 helps, it justifies further RNA-side exploration (scgpt, multiprofile); if it doesn't, PCA is near-optimal and effort should shift to other axes."
}

